          "kind": "informational",
          "level": "none",
          "guid": "mt0tfqkr47qxhhvc",
          "message": {
            "text": "Named attach (not imperative, not onMount) deliberately.\n\nimperative named a style, not a behavior. onMount was rejected for two reasons: (1) the node already exists when you call this — there is nothing to wait for, so \"mount\" misdescribes the timing; and (2) it would collide with remountOn's existing onMount(root) option in consumers' heads.\n\nThe distinguishing feature vs. a bare setup(node) call is the auto-teardown when the node leaves the document — so the name centers on the attach/detach lifecycle. Considered whileConnected (most literal) and bindNode/nodeScope (consistent with kerfjs/scope); attach won on call-site ergonomics and its match to connectedCallback/disconnectedCallback semantics.\n\nThe JSDoc also drops the prior \"useEffect-with-cleanup\" framing, which imported React associations that don't apply here (no dependency array, no re-run, no render-phase/hook-order scoping, no component-instance tie).\n",
            "markdown": "Named `attach` (not `imperative`, not `onMount`) deliberately.\n\n`imperative` named a *style*, not a behavior. `onMount` was rejected for two reasons: (1) the node already exists when you call this — there is nothing to wait for, so \"mount\" misdescribes the timing; and (2) it would collide with `remountOn`'s existing `onMount(root)` option in consumers' heads.\n\nThe distinguishing feature vs. a bare `setup(node)` call is the **auto-teardown when the node leaves the document** — so the name centers on the attach/detach lifecycle. Considered `whileConnected` (most literal) and `bindNode`/`nodeScope` (consistent with `kerfjs/scope`); `attach` won on call-site ergonomics and its match to `connectedCallback`/`disconnectedCallback` semantics.\n\nThe JSDoc also drops the prior \"useEffect-with-cleanup\" framing, which imported React associations that don't apply here (no dependency array, no re-run, no render-phase/hook-order scoping, no component-instance tie).\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/attach.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 39,
                  "endLine": 42,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "\n/**\n * Run `setup(node)` now, and its returned teardown once — when `node` leaves the\n * document, or when the returned disposer is called, whichever is first. Returns"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
